text:
maria gonzalez: Quick sync — I'm planning the audit event schema cutover from v2 -> v3 this week. PR is up but before I merge I need confirmation on RBAC implications, KMS column mapping, and whether we need customer-facing notices.

jonathan li: Can you summarize the breaking changes? Are we removing fields or renaming? Consumers will need adapters.

maria gonzalez: Main changes: remove `session_id` (deprecated), rename `actor_id` -> `actor.subject_id`, add `actor.type` (user/service/bot), add `data_classification` (PII/PII_HIT/NO_PI). We'll also add an `event_version` int and prefer `event_source.region`.

sara k: Quick note — validator tool (https://ci.internal/tools/audit-validator) ran against the PR and found 2 consumers failing on `actor_id` rename. Patch suggests an adapter shim but we should gate it.

infra-bot: CI: audit-validator: 2 failures (consumer: search-indexer, consumer: billing-bridge). Full report: https://ci.internal/reports/audit-v3-compat.html

jonathan li: RBAC: changing `actor_id` shape may affect our policy engine lookups. If we split id + type, we need to update the `rbac:resolve` calls and ensure rolebindings accept both old and new shapes during transition. Plan: support both shapes for 2 weeks behind a feature flag.

maria gonzalez: Agreed. Plan outline: 1) Add `event_version` header (Audit-Event-Version: 3) and dual-write v2+v3 for 7 days. 2) Enable consumer shim that maps `actor.subject_id` -> `actor_id` for legacy consumers. 3) Ramp traffic with canaries (10% -> 50% -> 100%) and monitor validator failures. 4) After 14 days and 0 critical fails, flip read path to v3-only and remove shim after 30 days.

ops eli: Backfill note: if we backfill `data_classification` for historical events we'll incur large egress/compute cost. Suggest we keep backfill optional for customers and provide a migration tool they can run on-demand.

legal team: We need to sign off on `data_classification` semantics before public rollout. If any event can contain PII, default retention and export controls must be enforced. Provide docs describing field values and retention behavior. Also we need a short customer notification template for customers relying on event payload contracts.

maria gonzalez: Will draft the legal doc and notification. Early draft of schema snippet below — please review quick: 

```json
{
  "event_version": 3,
  "event_type": "login.attempt",
  "timestamp": "2026-03-20T15:02:00Z",
  "actor": {
    "subject_id": "u_12345",
    "type": "user"
  },
  "data_classification": "NO_PI",
  "payload": { /* freeform */ }
}
```

jonathan li: Also callout: KMS change — when we write v3 events we want to include an encrypted `actor.affiliation` field. That will require a KMS key alias and new KMS policy so that dedicated/private customers can opt out. Who owns the KMS rollout?

sara k: I'm on KMS tasks. We need to add key rotation considerations and ensure HSM-backed keys for on-prem customers. For hosted we can default to `redwood-audit-v3` key; for Private we allow customer-managed key ARN. Update: created RFC PR with key policy template.

infra-bot: RFC PR created: github.com/redwood/rfcs/pull/834 — includes KMS policy and airflow migration playbook.

legal team: Add a short Q/A in the customer notice: will their old audit integrators break? Provide recommended adapter code snippet and timeline.

maria gonzalez: Good call. I'll attach an adapter example and a rollback checklist. Example adapter (JS) snippet: 

```js
// shim to convert v3 -> v2 for legacy consumers
function shimV3toV2(evt) {
  if (evt.actor && evt.actor.subject_id) {
    evt.actor_id = evt.actor.subject_id;
  }
  // drop new fields that v2 doesn't expect
  delete evt.data_classification;
  return evt;
}
```

ops eli: Monitoring: create a dashboard that tracks validator failures by consumer and error type, KMS encryption errors, and RBAC resolver errors. Set an alert when validator failures > 5% for 30m.

sara k: I'll add health checks to the validator and a per-consumer rate-limited retry for transient errors.

jonathan li: One more: telemetry headers. We should add `X-Audit-Migration-ID` to requests during canary so we can filter logs and attribute failures to the rollout.

maria gonzalez: Will add the header and the dashboard filters. Timeline proposal: start canary tomorrow 09:00 UTC, 3-day canary window with nightly validation runs, then expansion subject to legal signoff. Anyone blocking? :eyes: :warning:

legal team: Blocking until we finalize data classification and customer notice language. Can review today if you send the draft.

maria gonzalez: Sending draft in 30m. Thanks everyone — I'll update this thread with the final PR link and the release toggle name.

infra-bot: Deployment note: feature flag `audit.v3.dual_write` created (owner: @maria gonzalez).
